From 027330f33cc1f76da5e443c07fd4dc8a535c0fed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:07:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] input: add a keyboard driver for the NVIDIA embedded
 controller

The Toshiba AC100 (paz00) has its keyboard behind the NVIDIA embedded
controller ("nvidia,nvec"), the I2C bus master, which talks to a Tegra
I2C controller in slave mode. Poll that controller when the console looks
for input, as tegra-kbc does, and hand the PS/2 set 1 scan codes to the
input layer.

The EC keeps the state of its PS/2 port while the machine is off, and a
touchpad left streaming blocks the keyboard events, so the port is reset
before the keyboard is enabled.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/Kconfig               |   8 +
 drivers/input/Makefile              |   1 +
 drivers/input/nvec-keyboard.c       | 541 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/configs/tegra-common-post.h |   8 +-
 4 files changed, 557 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/nvec-keyboard.c

